  "result": "Perfect! All 111 tests pass. I've successfully added UTC-based date utilities to the invoicing system.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/dates.js** - New date utilities working entirely in UTC:\n   - `isValidDate(text)` - Validates YYYY-MM-DD format and ensures date is real (rejects Feb 30, etc.)\n   - `addDays(date, n)` - Adds n days to a date (positive or negative)\n   - `daysBetween(a, b)` - Returns whole days between dates (b - a)\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** - Updated date validation:\n   - Imported `isValidDate` from dates module\n   - Replaced inline date validation with `isValidDate()` call (cleaner, reusable)\n\n3. **test/dates.test.js** - Comprehensive test coverage:\n   - Valid and invalid date formats\n   - Non-existent dates (Feb 30, Apr 31, etc.)\n   - Leap year handling (Feb 29 in leap/non-leap years)\n   - Positive and negative day arithmetic\n   - Month and year boundaries\n   - Leap year calculations in day differences\n   - Large date ranges\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- All dates are YYYY-MM-DD strings\n- All operations use UTC (via `T00:00:00Z`)\n- Date validation checks both format and reality (prevents normalized dates like Feb 30 \u2192 Mar 2)\n- `daysBetween` returns whole days (no fractional days)",
